      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The prior art review flags US Patent 10,555,889 as a significant hurdle because it describes a \"Layered Carbon-Ceramic Composite for Heat Dissipation,\" which closely mirrors your SSTM's core composition. While your designation of \"solid-state\" and proprietary *method* of layering might offer differentiation, investors will immediately question novelty against this existing composite structure. You must clearly articulate what unique structural element or functional improvement your specific graphene-ceramic composite offers that is absent from Patent 10,555,889.",
      "source": "target",
