      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Focusing your patent claims on the *method* of achieving a superior thermal performance, rather than just the basic composition, is a viable strategy. By framing the invention around the specific process or the resultant performance metrics (thermal conductivity values unattainable by prior art), you create a functional barrier rather than just a structural one. This allows you to credibly claim a novel, non-obvious application, which can give you sufficient confidence to present a strong IP outlook to investors.",
      "source": "target",
